<title>THAILAND: Thai May foreign reserves fall to US$33.3 bln.</title>
<headline>Thai May foreign reserves fall to US$33.3 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's foreign reserves fell to US$33.3 billion in May from $37.3 billion in April, Virabongsa Ramangkura, a board member of the Bank of Thailand, said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    THAI FOREIGN RESERVES     May 97	April 97	May 96</p>
<p>					 33.3	   37.3	   39.1</p>
<p>Note - The reserve figures are in billion U.S. dollars.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
